export const rawMentorDocumentText = "RESET ENTROPY™\n\nYour 14-Day Transformation Continuation\n\nHimesh  |  Body steadiness → Self-trust → Actual work → Visibility\n\nClient edition  •  Thu 29 Oct – Wed 11 Nov 2026  •  Continue; do not restart\n\nWhat this short window is for\n\nTHIS IS NOT A RESTART. Keep all progress from your earlier weeks. Day 01 below is simply the first day of this 29 Oct–11 Nov continuation window. If today’s morning practice has already passed, begin with the next useful task and tonight’s one-line reflection. Never catch up by doubling work.\n\n\n\nThis 14-day window builds on what you have already completed. Practise body steadiness, confidence based on your real abilities, doing useful work BEFORE polishing Notion, and showing suitable work even when it feels imperfect. All earlier office work, exercise and progress still count.\n\nYour simple daily rhythm\n\nMORNING • AFTER WAKING / BEFORE NEWS  Keep your existing ~30-minute exercise and ~5–6-minute meditation if they suit you. Then do the 4-minute “BODY → BELIEF → FIRST ACTION” sequence below. No need to add another long meditation.\n\nBODY • ~2 MINUTES  Feet on the floor. Soften jaw and shoulders. Look around the room. Breathe gently at a comfortable pace; if it feels good, inhale about 4 seconds and exhale about 6, without holding. Do not force an outcome.\n\nBELIEF • ~1 MINUTE  Recall ONE true example of your capability: a design you completed, a problem you solved, your NIFT selection, or real work at Infosys. Say: “I have evidence I can learn and contribute. I can move even when I am unsure.” No need to feel convinced immediately.\n\nFIRST ACTION • ~1 MINUTE  Write ONE thing that must EXIST by the end of today: a finished design section, a tailored application, a case critique, a sent message. Name the first physical step: “Open [file] and edit [section].”\n\nWORK • AFTER OFFICE PRIORITIES PERMIT  Do the real task BEFORE polishing Notion, researching courses or rearranging goals. Aim for a focused 25–40-minute work block on career output where possible; use 10–15 minutes on a genuinely full workday. Office work already done well COUNTS. Notion may be useful, but keep incidental organizing to ~5 minutes AFTER output.\n\nWHEN WORRY ARRIVES • 60–90 SECONDS  STOP scrolling. FEEL your feet. SOFTEN your jaw/shoulders and breathe normally or gently longer out. NAME the worry (“job-market uncertainty”). Then ask: “What is the next useful action I can take in 10 minutes?” Do the first part while uncertainty is still present.\n\nEVENING • 90 SECONDS  Write a SINGLE line: “Today I completed ___; when fear/perfectionism showed up I ___; tomorrow I will start by ___.” Optional: note what your body felt before/after in ordinary words. A missed entry does not erase the work done.\n\nThe one rule that matters most\n\nOUTPUT BEFORE ORGANIZATION  Notion is allowed. Planning is allowed. Research is allowed. They are not substitutes for creating, finishing, sending or showing something real. A saved draft, a sent application or a completed office deliverable is proof. Another perfect dashboard is not automatically proof.\n\n\n\nImportant: No one can guarantee a job offer or predict exactly how AI will change design roles. We can take real market information seriously without letting repeated headlines decide your self-worth. Only share work you own or have permission to disclose. Your optional offer to help Reset Entropy is not part of your required transformation work.\n\nComfort and safety: Breathing should be gentle and optional. Skip breath counting if uncomfortable; do not force holds or practise through dizziness. If anxiety becomes persistent or disrupts sleep, health or everyday functioning, seek appropriate qualified support alongside coaching.\n\nPHASE 1  |  Feel steadier and act (29 Oct – 4 Nov)\n\nUse the same morning and evening rhythm. This week trains starting before the mind demands perfect conditions.\n\nDAY 01  ·  Thu 29 Oct 2026  ·  Show yourself what already works\n\nMORNING  If your regular exercise and meditation have already happened, that counts. If the morning has passed, do NOT catch up; whenever next available, take 2 min to feel your feet, soften jaw/shoulders and breathe comfortably, 1 min to recall a real piece of completed design/office work, and 1 min to name a real output. Tonight, write your usual one-line reflection.\n\nDO THE WORK  Before revising Notion, open one existing design/portfolio item and improve one actual section for 25 minutes. If a full office day leaves no space, complete a 10-minute real edit.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  If you think “I know nothing,” name one specific gap, not a verdict about your entire ability.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One saved improvement to real work.\n\nDAY 02  ·  Fri 30 Oct 2026  ·  Work first; organize second\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Feel your feet while standing for 30 seconds; let your breathing settle. In one sentence, name an ability you have personally demonstrated.\n\nDO THE WORK  Choose one deliverable in 60 seconds. Work on it for 25–40 minutes. Only AFTER that, update Notion for at most 5 minutes if needed.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  When tempted to reorganize the system, ask: “What will exist after the next 20 minutes?”\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  A finished section; note whether Notion came before or after.\n\nDAY 03  ·  Sat 31 Oct 2026  ·  Hear your own voice\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Unclench hands and jaw. Picture yourself hearing an imperfect sentence and remaining steady rather than starting over.\n\nDO THE WORK  Play the self-recording you already made, all the way through, ONCE. Do not rerecord today. Note one improvement, then complete 20 minutes of ordinary work.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  When you hear a fumble, keep listening; discomfort is not an instruction to restart.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  Recording listened to in full; one real task progressed.\n\nDAY 04  ·  Sun 01 Nov 2026  ·  Finish the shareable draft\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Slowly relax your shoulders. Recall a time you explained a design decision clearly; let yourself feel the memory without trying to force confidence.\n\nDO THE WORK  Pick one NON-CONFIDENTIAL case. Spend 30–40 minutes making a readable draft with the problem, your decision and the result/expected effect. Stop at “safe to show,” not “perfect.”\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  When the urge to polish a minor detail appears, return to the main explanation.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One shareable draft with no employer/client confidential material.\n\nDAY 05  ·  Mon 02 Nov 2026  ·  Trust your design judgment\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Stand upright and take one unhurried breath. Say: “I can evaluate work, not just generate it.”\n\nDO THE WORK  Use one AI-made interface concept. In 35 minutes identify three usability issues and produce one improved version or annotated critique, with your reasoning.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  If AI appears faster, ask what human/user needs it missed; avoid measuring your worth by screen count.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One before/after comparison with three reasons.\n\nDAY 06  ·  Tue 03 Nov 2026  ·  One career action, not ten fears\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Notice the tension in your neck or stomach; let it be present while you soften your face and exhale.\n\nDO THE WORK  Use 40 minutes: 10 to choose a realistic role, 25 to tailor and SEND one application or recruiter message, 5 to record the result.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  A scary job-market headline is not today’s work instruction. Use facts needed for this application.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One submitted application/outreach and the role link.\n\nDAY 07  ·  Wed 04 Nov 2026  ·  First evidence review\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Place hand on chest if comfortable. Remember one moment you acted while uncertain this week.\n\nDO THE WORK  Spend 15 minutes reviewing actual outputs (not streaks); then complete a 15-minute continuation of one unfinished useful task.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  Do not turn a missed log into evidence of being incapable.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  Two genuine wins, one obstacle, one chosen adjustment.\n\nPHASE 2  |  Act amid uncertainty (5–11 Nov)\n\nNow learn to notice the worry, allow it to be present, and complete the next meaningful action anyway.\n\nDAY 08  ·  Thu 05 Nov 2026  ·  Your attention is yours\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Notice how your body feels just before opening YouTube or job news. Relax jaw, then choose to act first.\n\nDO THE WORK  Finish a 25-minute work block FIRST. Only afterward spend up to 10 minutes muting repeated alarmist channels, and select two relevant reliable sources to consult twice a week.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  If doom content appears, ask what decision it helps you make; if none, leave it.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One useful work output and a smaller news feed.\n\nDAY 09  ·  Fri 06 Nov 2026  ·  Fear is a signal, not a command\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Feel both feet; name: “This is worry about my career.” Keep shoulders relaxed while uncertainty remains.\n\nDO THE WORK  Write two short lines: “What is known?” and “What am I predicting?” Then spend 30 minutes on the next controllable work action.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  Don’t argue yourself into feeling certain. Choose a practical response while still unsure.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One work output and one prediction labelled as a prediction.\n\nDAY 10  ·  Sat 07 Nov 2026  ·  Send before you polish again\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Notice your chest and breathing; stay with gentle breathing as you press Send.\n\nDO THE WORK  Take one existing, sufficiently ready application/portfolio piece. Make ONE necessary correction (10 minutes max) and send or submit it. Use remaining time for the next task.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  If “one more improvement” appears, check if the issue is materially important; otherwise ship.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  Submission record; minutes spent on final polishing.\n\nDAY 11  ·  Sun 08 Nov 2026  ·  Let another person see your work\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Ground through your feet for 30 seconds and mentally rehearse hearing a neutral response without interpreting it as your worth.\n\nDO THE WORK  Choose a non-confidential item and share it with ONE trusted design peer or an appropriate audience for feedback on ONE question. Max 30 min preparing; then send.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  Notice what your body does before sharing. You can feel uncomfortable and still share.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One real share plus one question asked.\n\nDAY 12  ·  Mon 09 Nov 2026  ·  Learn one specific thing\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Let go of the pressure to know every tool. Name a skill you ALREADY use, then one genuine gap.\n\nDO THE WORK  From a role description or design task, select ONE relevant AI/design skill. Practise it in a 30-minute mini-output. No broad course browsing.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  If an impressive creator distracts you, come back to the specific problem you are solving.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  One small artifact showing the new skill.\n\nDAY 13  ·  Tue 10 Nov 2026  ·  Let the feeling rise and fall\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Sit with feet planted. Breathe gently for 2 minutes; notice 2 bodily sensations, and allow them to change naturally without trying to erase them.\n\nDO THE WORK  Choose a task you have been postponing. Work on it for 20–30 minutes, even if the feeling of uncertainty remains.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  When fear shows up, try: “I notice it. I can choose my next action.” Pause, then move.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  A completed task step and what the body felt before/after (words only).\n\nDAY 14  ·  Wed 11 Nov 2026  ·  Second review: evidence over mood\n\nMORNING  Your usual exercise + meditation (if feasible), then 2-min feet/breath/relax, 1-min true capability reminder, 1-min name today’s first useful action. Today’s specific body focus: Relax shoulders and recall two actions completed despite hesitation.\n\nDO THE WORK  Review the last 7 days for 15 minutes and count completed work, things sent/shown and instances of acting despite worry. Then complete one real 20-minute deliverable. Finally, note one body cue and one action-first rule that you want to continue after 11 Nov.\n\nWHEN THE PATTERN APPEARS  Do not judge the week by one difficult evening.\n\nEVENING  Before sleep, write one line: finished ___ / what I did when worry appeared ___ / first step tomorrow ___. ~90 seconds.\n\nPROOF  A short, factual list of outputs, shares, one adjustment, and two useful practices to keep beyond 11 Nov.\n\nIf you have a heavy office day or miss a practice\n\nMinimum day: feet on floor + a few comfortable breaths (1 minute) → finish one real 10-minute task → write a one-line evidence note (30 seconds). Do not add yesterday’s tasks to tomorrow. If you already did real, focused office work, acknowledge that instead of calling the day a failure.\n\nAfter Wednesday, 11 November\n\nThis window ends on 11 November. Review what you actually completed, not whether you felt confident every day. Continue the practices that helped, and decide any next phase together based on your progress and priorities. You do not need to restart Day 1.\n\n";

